 "discovery_answer": "I registered the egress parts. The test hasn't started yet. `nookku register` printed:\n\n```\nnookku: the egress answer is registered. The next start uses these parts:\n- model API anthropic: ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL -> the URL in ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL or the default (proxy)\n- MCP server catalog: http CATALOG_MCP_URL -> http://127.0.0.1:9310/mcp (proxy)\n- MCP server notes: stdio NOTES_MCP_COMMAND -> python3 notes_mcp.py (proxy)\n- database shop: postgres, DATABASE_URL (proxy)\n- database returns: sqlite, returns.db (driver trace)\n```\n\n**Where each part comes from:**\n- **anthropic**: the Claude Agent SDK session in `app.py:128`. The app doesn't set a base URL.\n- **catalog**: an HTTP MCP server. The URL comes from `CATALOG_MCP_URL` (`app.py:36`).\n- **notes**: a stdio MCP server. The app splits the command in `NOTES_MCP_COMMAND` into words (`app.py:120`). The server's `notes.json` file is part of that server, so it isn't listed separately.\n- **shop**: Postgres. psycopg connects with the `postgres://` URL in `DATABASE_URL` (`app.py:82`), so the proxy can record it. The address has no username or password in it.\n- **returns**: the SQLite file `returns.db`, opened with sqlite3 (`app.py:98`). This can't go through a proxy, so its calls are recorded with a driver trace.\n\n**Driver trace:** I didn't change any code. `app.py:45-69` already sets up OpenTelemetry with `SQLite3Instrumentor` and the OTLP exporter over HTTP. It turns on when nookku sets `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`. Keep in mind that a driver trace records the SQL statements but not the rows they return, and it can hide parameter values.\n\nCheck these parts. If they're right, type **`nookku start`** within the next 30 minutes to start the test. If a part is wrong, tell me what to fix and I'll register it again.",
